      "content_sha256": "d6850606abed7f74f9d881a053102e96f5071c8dc79426c3cd091785d17adf4a"
    },
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "Design II has two particularly useful features. First, the variance components $ \\sigma_{s}^{2} $ and $ \\sigma_{d}^{2} $ are respectively equivalent to the covariances between paternal and maternal half sibs. This equivalency can be verified by referring to Equation 20.1a and recalling that only like terms (those with identical indices) are correlated,",
